to where people get down at."

00:28:18.738 --> 00:28:21.408
- Mmhmm
- "Like, you done got down there
 a couple times, too."

00:28:21.408 --> 00:28:25.203
But it's like, you know, you can go there,
and it's like if you're really walking in

00:28:25.203 --> 00:28:28.373
the way that you supposed to be walking
or you say that you're walking,

00:28:28.790 --> 00:28:31.167
you know, you can go there
and kinda, like, flip the script.

00:28:31.167 --> 00:28:34.045
You know, you can go there and be—you
can have a good time,

00:28:34.045 --> 00:28:37.173
have a good time more than
anybody else—and be sober.

00:28:37.340 --> 00:28:39.801
You know? There's
no limit to the fun that you can have,

00:28:39.801 --> 00:28:41.469
and you can just go about different

00:28:41.469 --> 00:28:43.471
things. Like, I've developed
a new relationship

00:28:43.471 --> 00:28:45.348
with, like, nature since I've been out here.
- Nice.

00:28:45.348 --> 00:28:47.350
- So it's just, it's just things like that.

00:28:47.392 --> 00:28:50.645
You can go about your business
differently, even though everybody around

00:28:50.645 --> 00:28:53.898
you may be going about it their way.

00:28:54.107 --> 00:28:55.442
- Mmhmm.
- You know, you don't have to do what they do.

00:28:55.442 --> 00:28:58.486
- Yeah. Are there things
that you avoid doing here?

00:28:59.821 --> 00:29:01.156
- I wouldn't necessarily avoid.

00:29:01.156 --> 00:29:02.907
I just, you know,

00:29:03.116 --> 00:29:05.618
I just create boundaries,
I guess? Like, I'm just like,

00:29:06.244 --> 00:29:08.788
ain't no reason for me to go to the club.
Like, I don't even enjoy the club.

00:29:09.330 --> 00:29:10.874
- Especially in Vegas. It's crazy.

00:29:10.874 --> 00:29:13.376
- If I'm going to the club,
I'm trying to please somebody else.

00:29:13.376 --> 00:29:14.794
- Yeah.
- Or I'm trying to be seen in front of other people.

00:29:14.794 --> 00:29:18.089
And it's like half the time I get there,
I could fall asleep, standing up in there.

00:29:18.548 --> 00:29:21.134
So it's like, I don't need to do that.

00:29:21.176 --> 00:29:22.051
I just don't need to do that.

00:29:22.051 --> 00:29:23.887
So it's like, I mean, clubs are the
only place where

00:29:23.887 --> 00:29:27.515
I'm like, "Yeah, I'm not going." Like, it just
doesn't, you know, make sense for me to be there.

00:29:27.515 --> 00:29:28.683
Like, it's just not how I'm moving.

00:29:28.683 --> 00:29:32.437
So I'll just say that.
- As someone who has been so open—

00:29:32.437 --> 00:29:36.566
and I feel like any football fan,
I mean, really any people fan, right?

00:29:36.566 --> 00:29:39.027
Like, just might know your story. It's
something you discuss a lot.

00:29:39.569 --> 00:29:43.114
Has that affected, like, romantic relationships

00:29:43.698 --> 00:29:47.285
in your experience? Like, just
everyone knows so much about you already?

00:29:47.285 --> 00:29:49.829
Is there like a hesitancy
sometimes for people?

00:29:49.829 --> 00:29:52.916
- I feel like it may, like, have people
like, "Whoa." Like, this

00:29:53.458 --> 00:29:54.834
may be a little scary for them.

00:29:54.834 --> 00:29:56.795
But I feel like that may be, like

00:29:57.754 --> 00:30:01.758
me, another way of me creating a boundary.
Like, if you not getting real

00:30:01.758 --> 00:30:02.926
like this or, like, you know,

00:30:02.926 --> 00:30:06.221
trying to be this open and vulnerable,
like, we ain't gonna be together.

00:30:06.221 --> 00:30:10.517
Like, I'm not finna be with somebody
that's out living how I used to live,

00:30:10.517 --> 00:30:16.397
you know? Cuz that could be a magnet to
attract me back to how I used to live, to my past.

00:30:16.397 --> 00:30:17.482
So it's just, you know,

00:30:17.482 --> 00:30:21.402
it just, it's a whole different standard
as far as dating now.

00:30:21.402 --> 00:30:22.862
It's just a lot has it go into it

00:30:22.862 --> 00:30:26.366
cuz it used to be, like, I would date
anybody that just wanted me or—
- Yeah.

00:30:26.699 --> 00:30:29.577
- You know what I'm saying? For, like,
that appreciation, that affection—
- Oh, to be a guy. [Laughing]

00:30:29.911 --> 00:30:33.665
- You know? And it's just like, you know
you deserve, you deserve better than that.

00:30:33.748 --> 00:30:36.334
- Yeah. No, absolutely.
So talk to me about now.

00:30:36.459 --> 00:30:38.086
What do you feel you deserve?

00:30:38.086 --> 00:30:38.837
Not just in relationships

00:30:38.837 --> 00:30:42.966
but, like, in life? Cuz you seem to have
this very strong sense of self, right?

00:30:42.966 --> 00:30:44.634
And what's right, what's wrong

00:30:44.634 --> 00:30:47.595
and what you need, what you want,
what you don't want, what you don't need.

00:30:47.679 --> 00:30:48.555
What does that look like for you?

00:30:48.555 --> 00:30:52.934
- You know, for me at this point,
it's just working towards, like, freedom,

00:30:52.934 --> 00:30:56.771
you know? Just freedom from what
other people think, freedom from,

00:30:57.188 --> 00:30:59.816
you know, my old thinking patterns,
because some of them still like

00:30:59.816 --> 00:31:00.608
to pop their way up.

00:31:01.818 --> 00:31:04.112
You know, just peace and serenity,

00:31:04.112 --> 00:31:06.197
you know? I don't need, I don't
need too much.

00:31:06.197 --> 00:31:09.075
I don't need, you know, the money
and all the extra stuff.

00:31:09.075 --> 00:31:13.037
You know, I just, meaningful connections
and relationships with people.
- Mmhmm.
- Like whereas

00:31:13.037 --> 00:31:17.250
before, you know, I would just sabotage
so many, and it's like I didn't feel like I deserved them.

00:31:17.292 --> 00:31:19.544
And now it's like, nah, I feel like I'm

00:31:19.544 --> 00:31:23.172
trying to develop myself in a way
where I can be loyal to somebody now.

00:31:23.172 --> 00:31:26.259
I can be, you know, there
where somebody can lean on me.

00:31:26.259 --> 00:31:30.555
It's not just about what I can get
from this, you know? So it's just

00:31:31.097 --> 00:31:33.057
little things like that,
just peace and serenity

00:31:33.057 --> 00:31:36.394
and just connection with other people.
Like, it's just those little things.
- Yeah.

00:31:36.728 --> 00:31:38.813
What stage of your life
would you say you're in right now

00:31:38.813 --> 00:31:42.233
if you had to title this
stage of your life?
